  "presentation_summary": [
    "Male patient with end-stage renal disease on outpatient hemodialysis via tunneled catheter presented with 2 days of nausea, vomiting, fever, and chills.",
    "At triage he was febrile to 103.3 F (39.6 C); admission labs included WBC 11.3 x10^9/L with 88.1% segmented neutrophils, glucose 283 mg/dL, BUN 57 mg/dL, and creatinine 6.57 mg/dL.",
    "One of two admission blood cultures grew Klebsiella pneumoniae resistant to carbapenems and many salvage agents; NDM was detected, while KPC, OXA, VIM, and IMP were not detected.",
    "The tunneled dialysis catheter was removed, repeat catheter-tip and blood cultures were negative, and the patient was discharged on aztreonam plus ceftazidime-avibactam."
